From f3dea5638be52a61ac33d5d2b34f3d3b8fb0b503 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:47:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep metadata-less PR reviews out of the
 ordering-dependency handoff

Problem: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dependency_review_no_verdict.py::
test_other_refusals_survive[missing] flaked on main (run 41531323842, job
125572639298) and wt/api-context-usage (run 41542995049): check_respawn_guard
returned None instead of "active_pr".

Why 1: active_pr_reason released the hold through _dependency_handoff_after,
not resumes_review. Proof: shifting the park 1 s past the PR comment fails the
test every time; the same shift with _dependency_handoff_after stubbed False
passes.
Why 2: the ordering handoff only looks at a park strictly after the newest PR
comment. The fixture used wall-clock time, so comment and park were usually in
the same second (a tie, held) and sometimes in consecutive seconds under runner
load (released).
Why 3: the handoff decides "this parent is a review, so resumes_review owns it"
only from verdict/approved/reviewed_sha keys or a VERDICT: line. A review that
completes with metadata {} and summary "Reviewed PR #682 ..." matches none of
them, so it counts as a finished ordering prerequisite and grants the
continuation that the exact-head review rule refuses.
Root (happened): the review/ordering classifier ignores the checkpoint's own
PR scope. In production the park is almost always >= 1 s after the PR comment,
so this refusal only held on same-second ties.
Root (not caught): parked() never pinned its chronology, so every review test
exercised the tie path on a fast machine. CI's flaky retry reported the run as
success.

Fix:
- kanban_dependency_review.is_review_result: also treat a parent result as a
  review when it names a checkpointed PR (pr / reviewed_pr key, or the PR URL
  or "PR #N" in its summary). A bare `head` is still not a review marker
  (operator gates record one: test_operator_added_gate_after_owner_park...).
- parked() pins publication at now-park_delay and the park at now, default 1 s
  (production order). The no-verdict refusal matrix runs at 0 and 1 s. The
  two sync tests whose clocks measure from publication pass park_delay=0.
- New boundary test: unreadable reviews that name the PR stay held. Ordering
  prerequisites that do not name it (including a {"head": sha} gate and an
  unrelated "PR #999") still get their one continuation.
---
